HST Office: no HST Base launcher anywhere; Base stays installed so that .odb files still open.

Owner decision (2026-11-11): users are offered HST Writer, HST Sheets and HST Slides only.
- scp2 folderitem_base.scp: the Windows Start menu entry "HST Base" (and its AppUserModelID property)
  is gone. A major upgrade removes the old product's shortcuts, so an older "HST Base" entry goes too.
  The .odb file type keeps its open command (program\sbase.exe -o).
- Common.xcu Menus/New: no "Database" item (private:factory/sdatabase). File ▸ New lists it no more,
  and neither does the macOS Dock menu nor the Windows tray menu, which show only the File ▸ New apps.
  The Start Center already has no Base button (hst-start-center-banner.patch).
- sysui base.desktop: NoDisplay=true. The launcher stays installed as the handler of .odb files
  (MimeType unchanged) but no app menu lists it. startcenter.desktop: no "Base" action.
macOS ships no Base launcher (scripts/macos/make-app-launchers.py builds Writer, Sheets and Slides).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_hide_base_launchers.py; scripts/linux/check-desktop-entries.py (Base hidden, .odb
handled); windows-smoke (scripts/windows/check-app-shortcuts.ps1: no "HST Base" shortcut after install,
upgrade or uninstall, .odb still opens with HST Office); scripts/macos/app-launchers-probe.sh (.odb opens).
